name 'designing-reliable-apps-preassessment-q12_2026'

question 'What happens when an error is thrown inside a try block?'

wrong 'The entire application stops running and displays a red error to the user'
wrong 'JavaScript automatically retries the code in the try block three times before giving up'
right 'Execution immediately jumps to the catch block, which runs its code instead of crashing the program'
wrong 'The try block finishes running all its remaining lines before passing the error along to catch'

allow_multiple_attempts true

